{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03O6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A\n\\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$A \\to\nA'$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$B' = B \\otimes_A A'$", "MATH_0006": "$A \\to A' = B$", "MATH_0007": "$A' = B \\to B' = B \\otimes_A B$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f4360964fa807f3159ea3b0b8df20e35d86af88cc8849e634f11c12b4f241312", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:adf36fbc1cb29b9f7f9997751e712b8491ba89e822951a4e181217812029e9c8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nGrothendieck proves this in three steps. Firstly, he assumes that the map <MATH_0001> has a section, and constructs an explicit homotopy to the complex where\n<MATH_0002> is the only nonzero term, in degree 0. Secondly, he observes that to prove\nthe result, it suffices to do so after a faithfully flat base change <MATH_0003>, replacing <MATH_0004> with <MATH_0005>. Thirdly, he applies the\nfaithfully flat base change <MATH_0006> and remark that the map\n<MATH_0007> has a natural section.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe same strategy proves the following lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5b2c5c48812f449ee707075b41aebe271090da0e71999b9edda2e042ac4d88a0", "unit_id": "tag:03O6:prose-0004"}
